      "id": 31180,
      "name": "Matchstickman",
      "username": "Matchstickman",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/matchstickman/{size}/1880_2.png",
      "created_at": "2012-05-22T11:05:57.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Are you doing something wrong? No. Some heroes are just maths heavy (Absolute Zero in particular).</p>\n<p>What you can do to help speed things up is to put coloured counters next to the cards that increase/decrease the damage, say red for ones that increase damage and green for ones that decrease damage. You could go further and have separate colours for ones that only effect heroes and ones that effect villains, or you could designate areas on the table for heroes and non-heroes and put the red/green counters in those areas and just count them up when you need to do damage.</p>\n<p>When the second edition of Sentinels comes out there will be a nice little sheet of tokens included or for those of us with first editions a picture file you can print out instead of using the non-official counters.</p>\n<p>If that option doesn’t take you fancy I seem to remember someone having similar problems on BoardGameGeek, wait here a second… <span class=\"hashtag\">#hold</span> music# … ah, here it is<br>\n<a href=\"http://www.boardgamegeek.com/thread/787209/the-omnitron-opus-the-struggle-to-evaluate-trackin\" data-bbcode=\"true\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">Thread</a><br>\nit talks about how one person went through various different solutions to try and track the damage modifiers; in the end they went with pen and paper! There’s a <a href=\"http://boardgamegeek.com/filepage/77824/sotm-game-tracker-one-sheet\" data-bbcode=\"true\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">file</a> that the guy made and uses as a tracker, you can give it a whirl and see if it makes things easier for you and your buddies.</p>\n<p>Hope something there helps</p>\n<p>EDIT:<br>\n<a href=\"http://www.boardgamegeek.com/image/1301465/oldschoolgamr\" data-bbcode=\"true\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">And a little token sheet he made to help out too</a></p>",
      "post_number": 3,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:05:08.648Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
